---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ImplementationExcerpt from "../components/ImplementationExcerpt.astro";
import ProjectList from "../components/ProjectList.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/portfolio";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Colin Vargas — computational combustion, CFD & aviation propulsion"
  description="I’m Colin Vargas. I’m looking for a Fall 2027 PhD group working on combustion, CFD, or aviation propulsion. Here’s what I’ve built and what I want to study next."
>
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="portfolio-home">
    <section class="portfolio-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-kicker">
        <span>aerospace engineering</span><span
          >looking for a fall 2027 PhD group</span
        >
      </div>
      <div class="hero-main">
        <div class="hero-identity">
          <h1 id="hero-title">
            colin<br />vargas<span class="accent-dot">.</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="hero-description">
            computational combustion<br />and aviation propulsion.
          </p>
          <p class="hero-bio">
            i love airplanes, and i keep coming back to what goes on inside
            the combustor. when do things like spray evaporation, turbulent
            mixing, and finite-rate chemistry actually change the answer you
            get from a simulation?
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button-link" href="/work/hydrogen-isooctane-equilibrium"
              >combustion case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
            ><a class="text-link" href="/resume"
              >technical profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
            ><a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}
              >email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-study">
          <ImplementationExcerpt animate />
          <a class="study-reference" href="/work/adaptive-cfd-solver"
            ><span>finite-volume advection</span><strong
              >see what i’ve built so far</strong
            ><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-index">
        <span
          ><i aria-hidden="true"></i> C++ / AMReX / MATLAB / NASA CEA</span
        ><a href="#selected-work"
          >jump to projects <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
    <section
      class="portfolio-section selected-work"
      id="selected-work"
      aria-labelledby="work-title"
    >
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span>projects</span><a href="/work"
          >all projects <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="section-intro">
        <h2 id="work-title">what i’ve worked on</h2><p>
          the fuel-blend study is closest to what i want to study next. the
          advection solver and mixing chamber show how i build and check models.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ProjectList limit={5} />
      <a class="index-link" href="/work/portfolio-and-technical-logs"
        ><span>software</span><strong
          >how i built this site</strong
        ><span>Astro / Git / project notes</span><span
          aria-hidden="true">↗</span
        ></a
      >
    </section>
    <section
      class="portfolio-section method-section"
      aria-labelledby="method-title"
    >
      <div class="method-grid">
        <div class="method-lead">
          <h2 id="method-title">how i check my work</h2><p>
            when a plot looks right, i still want to know what made it look
            that way. the mixing chamber was a good example. the temperature
            field looked plausible, but kinetic energy was still changing
            with the grid.
          </p><a class="text-link" href="/about"
            >more about me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </div>
        <ol class="method-list">
          <li>
            <span>01</span><div>
              <h3>start with the assumptions</h3><p>
                i write down what i’m leaving out and what i expect at the
                boundaries before i touch the solver.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>02</span><div>
              <h3>run a case i can check</h3><p>
                with periodic advection, i know where the scalar should end
                up and how much of it should still be there.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>03</span><div>
              <h3>write down how i got there</h3><p>
                i want to be able to come back to a plot and find the input,
                the code revision, and the checks that went with it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section
      class="portfolio-section beyond-section"
      aria-labelledby="beyond-title"
    >
      <div class="beyond-grid">
        <h2 id="beyond-title">flying and my homelab</h2><div>
          <p>
            i’m learning to fly, and i like tinkering with the server i run at
            home. you can see how the site, Minecraft relay, and storage are
            doing on my status page.
          </p><a class="text-link" href="/systems"
            >check my homelab <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="contact-plate" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span>fall 2027 PhD</span><a href="/resume">technical profile ↗</a>
      </div>
      <a class="contact-statement" href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}
        ><h2 id="contact-title">
          i’d love to hear<br />what you’re working on<span class="accent-dot">.</span>
        </h2><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
      <div class="contact-plate-bottom">
        <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
